---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **큰 한국 작품이 들어오면 다른 한국 작품이 밀려나나.** (`/crowding`)
 *
 * ── 왜 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   2026-08-09, `/hard-markets` 에 「한국 칸이 하나라 큰 작품이 그 칸을 가져간다」고 **안 재고 적었다.**
 *   그럴듯한 설명이었을 뿐이다. 그래서 잰다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **겉보기 수와 맞춘 뒤 수를 둘 다 낸다.** 맞춘 것만 내면 왜 맞췄는지가 안 보인다.
 * ⛔ **출발점 0 띠를 감추지 않는다** — 거기서는 효과가 없다. 이 주장의 반례가 표 안에 있어야 한다.
 * ⛔ 시장을 줄세우지 않는다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 * ⚠ 수를 손으로 적지 않는다. 전부 `wikitip-crowding.json` 에서 읽는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-crowding.json';

const 영띠 = d.bands[0];

const TITLE = 'When a Korean hit arrives, do the other Korean titles lose their places';
const DESC =
  `Across ${d.koreanArrivals.toLocaleString('en-US')} arrivals at the top three of a market chart, the other Korean titles `
  + `fall by ${Math.abs(d.koreanChange)} on average. Matched against the same measurement for `
  + `non-Korean arrivals at the same starting level, ${d.explainedByStartingLevelPc}% of that is where the chart started.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/crowding">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="note fine">{d.whyItWasAsked}</p>

  <section>
    <h2>The raw numbers, which cannot be read on their own</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Arrivals at the top {d.topRanks}</th><th>Cases</th>
          <th>Other Korean titles before</th><th>Change after</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="nm">Korean title arrives</td>
            <td>{d.koreanArrivals.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
            <td>{d.koreanBefore}</td>
            <td class="tot">{d.koreanChange}</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="nm">Any other title arrives</td>
            <td>{d.otherArrivals.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
            <td>{d.otherBefore}</td>
            <td class="tot">{d.otherChange}</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note"><b>{d.unit}</b></p>
    <p class="warn">{d.whyMatching}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="warn-box">
    <h2>The same measurement, with the starting level held fixed</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Other Korean titles before</th><th>Korean arrivals</th><th>Change</th>
          <th>Other arrivals</th><th>Change</th><th>Difference</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.bands.map((b) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{b.band}</td>
              <td>{b.koreanArrivals.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td>{b.koreanChange}</td>
              <td>{b.otherArrivals.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td>{b.otherChange}</td>
              <td class="tot">{b.gap}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="q">
      At the bottom row of the table there is no effect at all: a market with no other Korean title
      gains <b>{영띠.koreanChange}</b> after a Korean arrival and <b>{영띠.otherChange}</b> after any
      other, so the difference is {영띠.gap}.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Weighted to the same starting levels, the control falls <b>{d.matchedControl}</b> where the
      Korean cases fall <b>{d.koreanChange}</b>. What is left is{' '}
      <b>{d.excess}</b> — <b>{d.explainedByStartingLevelPc}%</b> of the raw gap of {d.rawGap} was the
      starting level, not the arrival.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>How this was counted, and what it cannot say</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Source</b> — {d.source}</li>
      <li><b>Rows read</b> — {d.rowsRead.toLocaleString('en-US')}.</li>
      <li><b>Window</b> — the {d.windowWeeks} weeks before against the {d.windowWeeks} weeks from
        the arrival, counting only the <i>other</i> Korean titles.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="warn">{d.cannotAnswer}</p>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/hard-markets">Which markets only take the wide titles</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/exit">How a title leaves</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/clumping">Not one a week</a> · <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/crowding" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  .warn-box { border-left: 3px solid #b45309; padding-left: 1rem; }
</style>
